@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Health

# Liveness check used by the smoke test; no database or model calls.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Chat page

# The chat page with the spec version picker (newest version selected).
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Ask

# Validate a question and return the fragment that opens the answer stream.
# No model calls: the graph runs when the stream below is opened.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

question=How does a client refresh an OAuth access token?&version=2026-07-28

###

# Search every spec version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

question=What changed in how servers declare tools?&version=all

### Answer stream

# Server-sent events: `stage` lines per graph step, `token` answer text as it is written,
# then `done` with the rendered answer. Runs the graph (3 model calls typically).
GET {{baseUrl}}/ask/stream?question=How%20does%20a%20client%20refresh%20an%20OAuth%20access%20token%3F&version=2026-07-28
Accept: text/event-stream

###

# Validation errors also arrive as a `done` event with status 200, so EventSource does not retry.
GET {{baseUrl}}/ask/stream?question=What%20is%20sampling%3F&version=1999-01-01
Accept: text/event-stream

###

# Validation: an unknown version returns a 422 error fragment without calling any model.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

question=What is sampling?&version=1999-01-01
